cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "This metadata describes an unreleased revision; verify the final immutable release and DOI before citing it."
title: "Declared Ambiguity: Fail-Closed Execution for Non-Idempotent Legacy APIs Without Idempotency Keys"
abstract: >-
  AEP is a fail-closed execution protocol for autonomous agents that call
  non-idempotent legacy APIs. Rather than claiming exactly-once semantics,
  it makes ambiguity a first-class, durable, detectable state: every external
  side effect is preceded by a durably-acknowledged write-ahead intent, every
  state write is fenced by lock ownership and exact expected-version CAS, and
  every unresolvable outcome halts and escalates rather than guessing. The
  honest guarantee on a single Redis instance is that corruption and
  contention are detectable and the system fails closed -- not absolute
  atomicity, not split-brain immunity, and not exactly-once delivery.
  This repository contains the protocol, baseline systems, fault-injection
  harness, tracked derived analysis products from a 432-run evaluation under
  real SIGKILL -- with a separate hard-Redis-kill ablation on one capability
  class, and a block-level write-loss probe on durable records rather than on
  protocol outcomes -- and the manuscript generated from them. The raw run
  archive is two parts, assembled and verified: the 2026-09-03 build (20
  collection roots, 1458 run directories, 26300 files, manifest SHA-256
  87fa2d534d8751d1239bd31f858a916536c94e1549741d37704a1b083d03e2d7) and a
  2026-09-15 extension (11 roots, 1332 run directories, 18494 files, manifest
  SHA-256 54d1ab0fc1e55283dc0aa1dabf121b047c432063d077074c3c45728735d63cd5).
  A Zenodo record is RESERVED under DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22766567: the
  identifier is fixed, the record is still a draft and the files are not
  uploaded, so it does not resolve yet. docs/29-archive-deposit.md is the
  checklist that publishes it, and lists this file among the sites to
  update when it does.
  ARTIFACT.md maps every quantitative claim in the paper to its
  currently available evidence and reproduction command.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hafizmirhamza276-lab/Research-paper-AEP"
